  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -26,17 +26,15 @@ This is the last release branch with official support for macOS 10.14 and 10.15.\n \n // The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-* wssalink:2025-04[] {notable}\n-MONGO dissector infinite loop.\n-wsbuglink:20724[].\n-cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: 1ec4709cab\n-// Fixed in release-4.6: fdb3823962\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: ac504cd5de\n-// Fixed in release-4.2: 513e5d4972\n+// * wssalink:2025-05[] {notable}\n+// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n+// wsbuglink:xxx[].\n+// cveidlink:2025-xxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: xxx\n+// Fixed in release-4.6: xxx\n+// Fixed in release-4.4: xxx\n // CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\n-// CWE-835\n-// * Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-09-22-11446760871.pcap. wsbuglink:20724[].\n+// CWE-824\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -45,12 +43,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark grabs your ID at 3 am, goes to Waffle House, and insults people.\n \n-* Using wslog parameters in command line applications leads to freeing invalid memory. wsbuglink:20500[].\n-* On macOS a lower resolution Wireshark icon is displayed in the App Switcher and Launchpad. wsbuglink:20544[].\n-// misdissection, but no crash.\n-* Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-08-06-10932469456.pcap. wsbuglink:20666[].\n-* Encoding on NAS5GS- NASDL Transport Message-Multiple Container contains inconsistencies. wsbuglink:20679[].\n-\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -70,12 +62,6 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // rg -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.14.. | rg packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-H.248E\n-HTTP2\n-IAX2\n-MONGO\n-NAS-5GS\n-XML\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n@@ -105,6 +91,7 @@ There is no updated file format support in this release.\n This document only describes the changes introduced in Wireshark {wireshark-version}.\n You can find release notes for prior versions at the following locations:\n \n+* https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.14.html[Wireshark 4.2.14]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.13.html[Wireshark 4.2.13]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.12.html[Wireshark 4.2.12]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.11.html[Wireshark 4.2.11]\n",
